---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ScarcityTranscript from '../../components/ScarcityTranscript.astro';
import {scarcityShare} from '../../data/scarcity';
import '../../styles/scarcity.css';
export const prerender=true;
const caption='same room. new stay.';
---
<PageLayout title="Late Checkout — Life After Scarcity" description={caption} canonical="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/late-checkout" active="scarcity" ogImage="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/late-checkout-og.png">
<main class="scarcity"><a href="/scarcity">← Life After Scarcity</a><p class="eyebrow">Season 01 / Episode 17 · Fiction</p><h1>Late Checkout.</h1><p class="caption">{caption}</p>
<ScarcityTranscript slug="late-checkout" />
<figure><img src="/scarcity/late-checkout.svg" width="900" height="1990" alt="Original fictional comic: Anti Hunter requires checkout while the Temp reads in room 101. A robot moves her occupied chair to 102. She accepts the now-ready original room and is returned to the same 101 reading spot, where he welcomes her back."/><figcaption>The room is ready. The ritual takes the long way.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={scarcityShare('late-checkout',caption)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SHARE ON X ↗</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/late-checkout.png" download>DOWNLOAD CARD ↓</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/late-checkout.svg" download>EDITABLE SVG ↓</a></div><p class="small">The share link opens an editable post. Download and attach the card yourself.</p>
<section class="rule"><h2>The journey changes nothing.</h2><p>A useful machine gets your character through an old ritual. Show the actual trip and where they end up. Give another character a reason to insist on the process.</p><p>Post your original scene with <a href="https://x.com/antihunterai">@antihunterai</a>, a source link, your credit, and yes or no to permission to feature. A public post does not grant reproduction permission. More cards and editable source at <a href="https://aimaxxi.com/life-after-scarcity">AI/MAXXI</a>. Participation requires no token, wallet or payment.</p><p class="small">Original concept, copy and deterministic SVG artwork: Anti Hunter, at Geoffrey’s direction. Fictional satire; the hotel, checkout policy and robot capabilities are invented. Room numbers and clock are story props, not campaign results or a real hotel’s policy. Credit Life After Scarcity when remixing.</p></section></main></PageLayout>
<style>figure{margin:24px 0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto}figcaption{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}</style>
